+2y & =500 \\\\ x & =500-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=500-2y$ in the expression $A=xy$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(500-2y)y \\\\ A & =500y-2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**: We solve the equation ${A}^{′}(y)=0.$ Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(y)=500-4y,\n$$\n\nand solving for the stationary points, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ 500-4y & =0 \\\\ 4y & =500 \\\\ y & =\\frac{500}{4} \\\\ y & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 6**: We confirm that $y=125$ is a maximum using the second derivative test. The second derivative is\n\n$$\n{A}^{″}(y)=-4\\,⟹\\,{A}^{″}(125)=-4<0.\n$$\n\nSince ${A}^{″}(125)$ is negative, we conclude that $y=125$ is indeed a maximum of $A(y).$\n\nFinally, when $y=125$, we have \n\n$$\ny=500-2(125)=250.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the dimensions of the field with the largest area are $x=250$ and $y=125,$ and we conclude that\n\n$$\nA=xy=250\\cdot 125=31\\,250.\n$$" 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355602 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355603 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355604 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355605 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355606 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1041 "selection" 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355606 13194139535570 true] [17592186355601 1110 #uuid "2044b0dd-ff1a-5da5-8a40-c8a4fe74c7ae" 13194139535570 true] [17592186355602 1034 "21\\,875\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" 13194139535570 true] [17592186355602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535570 true] [17592186355602 1111 #uuid "bd4fc09b-a1f6-558d-81c1-4761e11d87ff" 13194139535570 true] [17592186355603 1034 "56\\,875\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" 13194139535570 true] [17592186355603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535570 true] [17592186355603 1111 #uuid "3b8bfea8-0a20-5486-91a9-7d848